WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.099 --> 00:00:01.099
OK.

00:00:01.099 --> 00:00:03.060
Let's get right into audience questions for
the week.

00:00:03.060 --> 00:00:07.681
First one is, hey, David, we've seen all sorts
of different takes and plans from Donald Trump

00:00:07.681 --> 00:00:12.980
to governors about how and when states could
start to reopen after the virus.

00:00:12.980 --> 00:00:16.670
What should a reasonable reopening America
plan look like?

00:00:16.670 --> 00:00:18.040
So a couple of things on this.

00:00:18.040 --> 00:00:23.960
Number one, I don't have any independent knowledge
in the sense that I believe we should trust

00:00:23.960 --> 00:00:27.869
medical experts and public health experts
on this.

00:00:27.869 --> 00:00:32.230
And so I'm going by what those individuals
are saying.

00:00:32.230 --> 00:00:33.870
Not by what politicians are saying.

00:00:33.870 --> 00:00:36.899
I think there's one other element to this
that's important.

00:00:36.899 --> 00:00:42.979
In an ideal world, we would have done sort
of like a full shut down probably around February

00:00:42.979 --> 00:00:43.979
20.

00:00:43.979 --> 00:00:49.199
It could have gone to four months and it would
have been over this week and we would be in

00:00:49.199 --> 00:00:50.679
much better shape right now.

00:00:50.679 --> 00:00:57.519
Hindsight is 20/20, but the point is there
is a limited political willingness to continue

00:00:57.519 --> 00:01:03.539
expending political capital as the protests
mount and the demands mount, as crazy as the

00:01:03.539 --> 00:01:10.259
demands of the protesters are, as irrelevant
as those demands are to public health issues.

00:01:10.259 --> 00:01:16.700
The reality is the pressure is going to grow
and it's not going to be possible to open

00:01:16.700 --> 00:01:17.700
nothing.

00:01:17.700 --> 00:01:22.280
So I'm starting from the point of not what
is or would have been the safest.

00:01:22.280 --> 00:01:28.670
But what makes sense, given that the pressure
to reopen at least parts of society will only

00:01:28.670 --> 00:01:29.799
continue to grow.

00:01:29.799 --> 00:01:31.580
No one is testing now.

00:01:31.580 --> 00:01:35.329
I'm not going to get into the full back and
forth about how Donald Trump initially took

00:01:35.329 --> 00:01:39.530
took credit for testing, even though the testing
was terrible.

00:01:39.530 --> 00:01:44.689
He would insist that it's all him now, that
it's clear the testing is not up to par to

00:01:44.689 --> 00:01:45.689
reopen.

00:01:45.689 --> 00:01:48.329
Trump is saying governors have to figure out
this testing thing.

00:01:48.329 --> 00:01:50.610
Let's ignore the shirking of responsibility
for a moment.

00:01:50.610 --> 00:01:52.280
We don't have enough testing.

00:01:52.280 --> 00:01:56.340
We need, at a bare minimum, five hundred thousand
tests today.

00:01:56.340 --> 00:01:57.340
More.

00:01:57.340 --> 00:02:01.450
Most roadmaps say we need more, including
like a million tests today.

00:02:01.450 --> 00:02:06.200
Remember that with a million tests today,
it still takes you almost a year to test everybody.

00:02:06.200 --> 00:02:10.210
One roadmap says we need 22 million tests
today so you can test everybody on a rolling

00:02:10.210 --> 00:02:12.950
14 day roughly basis.

00:02:12.950 --> 00:02:17.570
Certainly five hundred or six hundred thousand
tests a day must be in place.

00:02:17.570 --> 00:02:23.150
But not only that, you need proper contact
tracing infrastructure in Massachusetts.

00:02:23.150 --> 00:02:26.730
Here, they've been hiring work from home,
contact tracers.

00:02:26.730 --> 00:02:28.670
Different health systems have been doing it.

00:02:28.670 --> 00:02:30.990
I think it pays around twenty five dollars
an hour.

00:02:30.990 --> 00:02:32.310
Work from home.

00:02:32.310 --> 00:02:38.441
All states need to be hiring proper contact
tracers so that you increase testing as you

00:02:38.441 --> 00:02:42.680
test a lot of people as soon as you get a
positive test.

00:02:42.680 --> 00:02:46.900
Contact tracing comes in and lets individuals
that may have been in contact with that infected

00:02:46.900 --> 00:02:52.230
person know so that they can quarantine then
all the stuff about phases.

00:02:52.230 --> 00:02:55.900
I'm not going to go piece by piece through
Donald Trump's proposal because I've already

00:02:55.900 --> 00:02:56.900
done it.

00:02:56.900 --> 00:02:57.900
But a few thoughts on that.

00:02:57.900 --> 00:03:01.070
Number one, there won't be a light switch
that's flipped.

00:03:01.070 --> 00:03:08.080
And we are back on some of the earlier things
that should happen include what retail elements

00:03:08.080 --> 00:03:12.850
can start to be opened up somewhat so that
they can recover some of their revenue.

00:03:12.850 --> 00:03:15.230
Remember, we've got the paycheck protection
plan.

00:03:15.230 --> 00:03:16.230
But the money ran out.

00:03:16.230 --> 00:03:20.320
So there's a ton of restaurants and other
retail facing businesses that risk going completely

00:03:20.320 --> 00:03:21.670
out of business.

00:03:21.670 --> 00:03:27.670
What can be done in restaurants in terms of
can people sit at tables, outback very much

00:03:27.670 --> 00:03:33.470
spaced out so that they feel like they've
had a dining experience, but the bag of food

00:03:33.470 --> 00:03:36.220
is placed on the table as if it were takeout.

00:03:36.220 --> 00:03:37.810
There's no interaction with the waitstaff.

00:03:37.810 --> 00:03:41.310
Would that make people feel as though we're
moving in the right direction, even though

00:03:41.310 --> 00:03:45.390
in practice it wouldn't change that much about
the risk exposure?

00:03:45.390 --> 00:03:46.390
I don't know.

00:03:46.390 --> 00:03:48.250
I'm just sort of thinking out loud here.

00:03:48.250 --> 00:03:50.890
Schools this semester should not reopen.

00:03:50.890 --> 00:03:52.570
It just doesn't make any sense.

00:03:52.570 --> 00:03:59.380
We should focus on shooting for the fall,
but being prepared to do the fall online.

00:03:59.380 --> 00:04:03.490
People who can work from home and who work
office jobs where a lot of the work is e-mail

00:04:03.490 --> 00:04:07.150
and phones should not go back to work anytime
soon.

00:04:07.150 --> 00:04:13.710
We should keep as many people home as is possible
to lower the risk of loosening up some of

00:04:13.710 --> 00:04:15.070
the public elements.

00:04:15.070 --> 00:04:17.040
Jim's probably can't open right away.

00:04:17.040 --> 00:04:20.630
I know that that was included in phase one
of Trump's plan.

00:04:20.630 --> 00:04:21.870
Does not seem reasonable.

00:04:21.870 --> 00:04:25.650
Seems like just an absolute cesspool of germs.

00:04:25.650 --> 00:04:31.520
And even if you maintain social distancing
in gyms, I don't see how you avoid gyms becoming

00:04:31.520 --> 00:04:32.670
a center of spread.

00:04:32.670 --> 00:04:39.940
While we have cases and we probably can't
really loosen travel anytime soon either.

00:04:39.940 --> 00:04:47.030
So for me, the the immediate loose innings
would be we start to let people get back to

00:04:47.030 --> 00:04:48.880
being a little bit social.

00:04:48.880 --> 00:04:54.800
Ideally, what we're talking about is, you
know, a couple that's been self isolating

00:04:54.800 --> 00:04:57.030
and another couple that's been self isolating.

00:04:57.030 --> 00:04:58.351
Get together in a.

00:04:58.351 --> 00:05:00.660
House and everybody.

00:05:00.660 --> 00:05:04.980
You don't shake hands, but you can hang out
a couple of hours.

00:05:04.980 --> 00:05:08.620
That probably would be like a next step as
cases go down.

00:05:08.620 --> 00:05:13.380
Again, some of these things of, you know,
maybe restaurants could figure out a way if

00:05:13.380 --> 00:05:18.340
they're large enough, you reduce the capacity
by 80 percent and you let people without table

00:05:18.340 --> 00:05:21.440
service just sit and have their takeout in
the restaurant.

00:05:21.440 --> 00:05:24.860
These are the types of things that that need
to happen.

00:05:24.860 --> 00:05:30.010
And then we want to start opening up some
other retail type businesses that may have

00:05:30.010 --> 00:05:31.010
been closed.

00:05:31.010 --> 00:05:32.220
But again, remember, many of those have been
open.

00:05:32.220 --> 00:05:34.810
A lot of stuff hasn't actually been closed.

00:05:34.810 --> 00:05:37.850
It's just been diminished.

00:05:37.850 --> 00:05:41.110
And people are having to, you know, wear masks
when they are inside.

00:05:41.110 --> 00:05:43.130
But those are some of the first steps I see.

00:05:43.130 --> 00:05:48.350
But really, the steps that need to happen
before anything is actually opened is testing

00:05:48.350 --> 00:05:53.410
that needs to increase dramatically and contact
tracing needs to increase them dramatically

00:05:53.410 --> 00:05:54.342
until we have that opening is a real risk.

